      summary: 'Create a home page and a supplies page with a list. Link the pages to each other.',
      explanation: [
        "A website can contain several HTML documents. Each document is a separate file, even when the pages look similar. A link joins them by giving the browser a path. A path tells it where to look for a file. index.html is often the name of the starting page; it is still an ordinary HTML file. Putting another filename in a paragraph only shows those words. To make navigation, put the filename in an a element's href. The destination file must exist at that location, and the spelling must match.",
        'Save this example as index.html. It is a complete home page for a different hobby.\n' +
          '\n' +
          '```html\n' +
          '<!doctype html>\n' +
